(Course Notes - Arrays and Linked Lists) Tj
() Tj T*
(An array stores elements in contiguous memory.) Tj T*
(Index access is O\(1\): the address of element i is base + i * size.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A linked list stores nodes with a value and a pointer to the next node.) Tj T*
(Insertion at the head is O\(1\), but there is no random access - reaching) Tj T*
(element i costs O\(i\).) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Choose arrays when you read by index often; choose linked lists when you) Tj T*
(insert or delete at known positions frequently.) Tj T*
ET
