(Course Notes - Stacks, Queues and Hash Maps) Tj
() Tj T*
(A stack is LIFO: push adds to the top, pop removes from the top.) Tj T*
(Typical uses: undo history, expression evaluation, DFS.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A queue is FIFO: enqueue adds at the rear, dequeue removes from the front.) Tj T*
(Typical uses: task scheduling, BFS, buffering.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A hash map hashes each key into a bucket. Average lookup, insert and) Tj T*
(delete are O\(1\); worst case is O\(n\) on collisions. A good hash function) Tj T*
(and a sensible load factor keep buckets short.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
